MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_001: Hm...
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_002: Hey, Big Promise! What are you doing here?\nJust...staring around the city?
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_003: <NCA>"It seems this city's spirit is returning..."
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_004: Well, right. There are more people here. But I've\ngot to say, still looks pretty rough to me.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_005: And people come only because their villages were\ndestroyed. So, they're at each other's throats.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_006: And there are a lot of kids here...without families.\nIt's, uh, like how I grew up in Breston.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_007: Town was a mess. No king around to make it better.\nThe back alleys were crawling with kids like me.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_008: Oh... Mm.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_009: It's actually worse here, to tell you the truth, and\nI still hate thinking about Breston.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_010: But if it's like this here, it's way worse than this\neverywhere else in the world.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_011: We've got to take care of all of the gates of the\nunderworld—fast as we can.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_012: Heeey, Loretta!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_013: Whoa! What's wrong? One of you guys get hurt\nor something? I hope no one's crying...
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_014: Nah, nothin' like that. It's a good day! I'm helpin'\nwith the...whaddayacallit...reconstruction!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_015: I got some food. I wanna share it with you!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_016: Aw, good job. And thanks, but I'm OK. You share\nthat with your friends, alright?
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_017: Hey, Big Promise... You know, I've been taking\ncare of him and some other kids lately.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_018: Sharing food. Hanging out. It started with him, then\nhis sister and all his friends...
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_019: I didn't want them to feel, you know...alone.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_020: <NCA>"That's extraordinary, Loretta."
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_021: Heh. Really? You think so? I've been weirdly...weird\nabout it all.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_022: Someone like me, a kid from the street... I used to\njust steal everything. Who do I think I am here?
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_023: <NCA>"You're someone who can help lots of children."
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_024: <NCB>"You can help everyone with your skills."
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_025: <ACA>Nah, I doubt it. I'm lucky they even let me help\nthem. We just kind of hit it off, that's all.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_026: <ACB>Help everyone? I'm not like you. I can't do\namazing things.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_027: But, maybe... Maybe there is stuff I can do to help.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_028: Anyway, I'll chew on it. I would like to help out\nthose kids if I can.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_029: No matter what, Balor's gotta go—quick as we\ncan get rid of him.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_A_030: Then we can really get down to work. Come on,\nBig Promise. Let's get this done.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_001: Huh? Ngh!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_002: Mmm... Hm?
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_003: Wh-what? Is...is that you...Big Promise?
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_004: *sob* It's you! It's REALLY you! You're baaack!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_005: <NCA>"What...what's going on?"
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_006: I was pretty sure you weren't coming back from\nthe underworld. But if you did, it'd be here!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_007: Th-then you NEVER came back! And I couldn't...\nI couldn't...stop cryyying!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_008: <NCA>"You exhausted yourself...crying?"
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_009: Hey! Sh-shut up! It's your fault you made me\nworry so much!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_010: This whole time here... I've been thinking about\nthat thing you said a ways back.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_011: About what I could put my mind to, if I wanted to.\nI think...I'm ready to do that.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_012: For all the kids here alone, no families to take care\nof them... I'm going to start an orphanage.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_013: I've decided that I can do a lot more, and really\nmake a difference!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_014: B-but then you never came back! I thought I'd\nnever get a chance to tell youuu!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_015: Awww, come on, Loretta. Get it together already!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_016: This isn't helping anyone!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_017: Big Promise came back. I've got a mission. And\nI've got to get on it!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_018: <NCA>"That's the spirit, Loretta."
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_019: <NCB>"You got it together..."
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_020: <ACA>Well, I kind of have to, right? There's a lot of kids\nout there who need help.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_021: <ACB>Yeah, yeah... Well, the kids will just worry about\nme if I keep gettin' all blubbery.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_022: <ACB>I'm the closest thing they're gonna get to a\nparent. I've got to start being a good example.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_023: But between you and me...I don't know where to\nstart. I'm totally clueless!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_024: Hey, don't laugh... Trying to be honest here...\nI've got a lot to learn.
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_025: <RSDS>Hey, Big Promise! If you've got so many opinions,\nhow about you come help me out?
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_026: Yeah! I'm going to build the best orphanage in\nthe world—and you're going to work for me!
MID_SE_Ism_Lor_S_027: And if you feel like up and vanishing again?\nI will never forgive you. You hear me?